Split the native linkage out of the endpoint features

Upstream commit series on marcomq/mq-bridge feature/dynamic-c-linkage,
rebased onto v0.4.11.

`full` used to mean one thing: every endpoint, with every C library
compiled from vendored sources. That is right for `cargo add mq-bridge
--features full`, and wrong for a distro or conda-forge package, where a
security fix to librdkafka has to reach the binary through a rebuild
rather than through a new upstream release.

The endpoint list therefore moves to `full-common`, and the two variants
are `full-common` plus a linkage:

    full          = full-common + ibm-mq + link-static  + vendored-protoc
    full-dynamic  = full-common + ibm-mq + link-dynamic

`link-static` is empty — it is the absence of `dynamic-linking`, named so
the two are visibly exclusive; src/lib.rs rejects the pair. `link-dynamic`
turns on `rdkafka?/dynamic-linking`, so librdkafka is found through
pkg-config instead of built from rdkafka-sys' vendored copy.

Only librdkafka is affected. SQLite stays bundled and is now pinned that
way in both variants: sqlx's `sqlite-bundled` and `sqlite-unbundled` hand
libsqlite3-sys two conflicting build strategies, so exactly one has to be
chosen, and bundling is the one that needs neither a libsqlite3 on the
system nor the libclang that generating bindings against one would
require.

Naming `sqlite-bundled` rather than the `sqlite` alias also drops the
alias' `sqlite-deserialize`, `sqlite-load-extension` and
`sqlite-unlock-notify` extras, and `default-features = false` drops sqlx's
`macros`, `migrate` and `json` — none of which this crate uses. The `any`
driver it does use is listed explicitly.

`vendored-protoc` gates the `protoc-bin-vendored` build-dependency that
`grpc` used to pull in unconditionally. `full` keeps it, so a bare
checkout still needs nothing installed; `full-dynamic` drops it, because a
packaged build must compile against the protobuf it ships.
